# .dockerignore - controls what files get sent to the Docker daemon as the
# build context when you run "docker build". Files/patterns listed here are
# excluded from that context (not sent, not usable by COPY/ADD).

# Note: Dockerfile is listed below even though it's always read directly
# from disk by the Docker client to determine build steps - it doesn't
# need to be in the context for the build to work. We exclude it here just
# so it never gets copied into the image accidentally (e.g. if a future
# COPY . . step is added).

# NOTE: "goserver" is intentionally NOT listed here.
# Your Dockerfile does `COPY goserver /bin/goserver`, so it must remain
# available in the build context, even though it's gitignored separately.

# --- Version Control ---
# Git metadata - large, and never needed inside the image
.git

# --- OS / Filesystem Metadata ---
# macOS folder view preferences
.DS_Store
# Windows thumbnail cache
Thumbs.db
# Windows folder display settings
desktop.ini

# --- IDEs & Editors ---
# Personal VS Code settings - local to your machine, not the build
.vscode/
# JetBrains (GoLand) project settings
.idea/
# Vim/Unix swap files
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Local Environment Secrets ---
# DANGER: never send credentials into the build context
.env
.env.*
# Private keys and certificates
*.pem

# --- Logs & Runtime Artifacts ---
# Local logs and crash dumps - irrelevant to the running app
*.log
*.crash

# --- Go Testing & Performance Profiles ---
# Not needed inside the image - only relevant during local development
*.out
*.coverprofile
*.pprof

# --- Documentation ---
# Not needed for the app to run
*.md

# --- Docker Meta Files ---
# The Dockerfile and this file don't need to be copied into the image
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore

# --- Python Artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# --- Python Virtual Environments ---
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
